  "event.region": "· region",
  "help.1.body": "PiMotionCam is a motion-detection recording service built on libcamera/picamera2. It provides live preview, motion-triggered recording, event playback and on-page tuning.",
  "help.1.title": "Overview",
  "help.2.body": "Motion is detected with frame differencing running two algorithms in parallel: the far algorithm targets small, slow objects in the distance, the near algorithm targets large objects up close. Every motion region is judged independently, and regions can be drawn on the preview image and named for reuse.",
  "help.2.title": "Motion detection",
  "help.3.body": "When motion triggers, the frames buffered by the pre-record window are written out first, recording then continues for the post-record duration, and the whole clip is finally encoded to H.264 MP4 by ffmpeg, together with a full-frame thumbnail and a cropped thumbnail of the moving object.",
  "help.3.title": "Recording",
  "help.4.body": "Commands can run on a weekday-and-time schedule or at a fixed interval. A command may be an internal command (record on, tl_start 30, ...), or any shell command when it is written in ~/.pikrellcam/at-commands.conf; the web command box only accepts internal commands.",
  "help.4.title": "Scheduled commands",
  "help.5.body": "Pan-tilt servos are driven through RPi.GPIO or ServoBlaster. Position presets can be saved, and the pan/tilt travel limits plus a smoothing time can be configured.",
  "help.5.title": "Servo",
  "help.6.body": "Use 'systemctl --user status pikrellcam-lite' to check the service state and 'journalctl --user -u pikrellcam-lite -f' to follow the live log.",
  "help.6.title": "Operations",
  "help.7.body": "Enable audio and select a microphone on the Media tab to save event and loop recordings as MP4 with AAC sound, including the matching pre-roll audio. Use the live meter to check capture. The preview countdown shows the time remaining in the current event or loop segment.",
  "help.7.title": "Audio and recording countdown",
  "help.8.body": "Loop recording splits video into timed segments, yields to motion events and resumes afterwards. Old loop segments are reclaimed first when a disk limit is reached. Unavailable external storage pauses recording or uses the configured fallback. Media counts and usage may take up to three seconds to refresh; filesystem free space is read live.",
  "help.8.title": "Loop recording and storage",
  "help.9.body": "Use the top bar to switch between Simplified Chinese and English; your choice is saved automatically. The project README provides a bilingual overview and links to the complete Chinese and English user guides.",
  "help.9.title": "Language and documentation",
  "hint.anyShell": "; entries in ~/.pikrellcam/at-commands.conf may be any shell command, while the web command box only accepts internal commands.",
  "hint.audioBackend": "Audio is captured through ALSA and muxed into the MP4 as an AAC track (the video itself is not re-encoded). Without a microphone this section can be ignored — recording works as usual.",
  "hint.currentState": "Current state: ",
  "hint.diskGuard": "The disk limit is a media quota and may be set up to 128 GB (larger than the whole disk is fine). What really protects you is the free-space floor: below it the oldest recordings are removed automatically, and recording is paused if that is not enough.",
  "hint.dragRegions": "Drag on the image to draw detection regions",
  "hint.drawRegionsLong": "Hold the left mouse button and drag on the image to draw a rectangle; click a region in the list on the right to select it — once selected you can drag the box, resize it from the small corner handle, and double-click it to rename.",
  "hint.imagingAwb": "White balance preset; a fixed preset helps at night",
  "hint.imagingAwbGains": "Manual red/blue gain; 0 means automatic",
  "hint.imagingBackend": "Each capture path supports a different set of parameters: on the ISP hardware path the imaging settings are applied when the capture process starts, so a change restarts the camera; libcamera and USB apply them live.",
  "hint.imagingBrightness": "Overall brightness; 50 is normal",
  "hint.imagingContrast": "Contrast strength; 0 is normal",
  "hint.imagingDenoise": "Noise reduction; useful in low light",
  "hint.imagingEv": "Auto exposure compensation in stops",
  "hint.imagingExposure": "Exposure strategy; sport shortens the exposure",
  "hint.imagingIso": "Fixed ISO gain; 0 means automatic",
  "hint.imagingMetering": "How auto exposure meters the scene",
  "hint.imagingSaturation": "Colour intensity; 0 is normal, -100 is pure greyscale",
  "hint.imagingSharpness": "Edge sharpening; 0 is normal",
  "hint.imagingShutter": "Fixed shutter time in microseconds; 0 means automatic",
  "hint.imagingZoom": "Digital zoom (crops and enlarges); resolution is lost",
  "hint.internalCommands": "Internal commands: ",
  "hint.loopYield": "Loop recording and event recording share the same hardware encoder and cannot run at the same time: when motion is detected the loop yields to the event clip and resumes afterwards. When the usage cap is exceeded the oldest loop segments are deleted first; event recordings are never touched.",
  "hint.placeholders": "Available placeholders: ",
  "hint.releasesKept": "Every version is kept separately under",
  "hint.restartOnChange": "Changing resolution or frame rate restarts capture",
  "hint.rollback": "— to roll back, point the",
  "hint.stopService": "After stopping, the picture and detection stop. Restart the service to resume.",
  "hint.storageSafety": "Safety: by default recording is paused when the external storage is removed instead of silently writing back to the SD card — otherwise long runs fill up the system partition and the device stops booting.",
  "hint.symlinkBack": "symlink back to the old version.",
